# Line-ending policy — LOAD-BEARING, do not remove.
#
# This repo's test strategy rests on BYTE-EXACT markdown fixtures and goldens:
# `init-templates.parity`, `lint-parity`, `bootstrap.parity`, `status.parity`,
# `r5-parity` and `smoke` compare generated markdown against committed fixtures,
# and `src/init-templates.ts` / `src/status.ts` normalise CRLF->LF internally but
# the COMPARISON is byte-for-byte.
#
# Without this file, a fresh clone on a machine with the common Windows setting
# `core.autocrlf=true` materialises every fixture with CRLF, and those six specs
# fail even though nothing in the code changed. Measured: a fresh clone produced
# `Test Files 6 failed | 41 passed (47)` with 8 failing tests, all in
# fixture-reading specs, while the same commit was green in the working tree.
# `git add` even warns "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it".
#
# `eol=lf` here overrides core.autocrlf for matching paths, so checkouts are LF
# everywhere and the goldens stay byte-exact.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows command scripts are the one place CRLF is conventional. The linter and
# every parity spec ignore them, so this cannot affect a golden.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary-ish assets must never be text-normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
